; Sprites written as pictures. A picture is a list of strings, one per row of
; pixels, each character a logical colour: . 1 2 3. The bytes come out the
; way PIPELINE stores sprites (and MODE 5 lays out the screen inside a
; character cell): a column four pixels wide at a time, top to bottom, then
; the next column to the right.

; The MODE 5 byte for four pixels: pixel n (0 leftmost) keeps its colour's
; high bit in bit 7-n and its low bit in bit 3-n.
FUNCTION mode5_byte(pixels)
    p = FIND(CODES(".123"), CODES(pixels))
= SUM((p DIV 2) * {128, 64, 32, 16} + (p MOD 2) * {8, 4, 2, 1})

; One character a pixel.
MACRO SPRITE_COLUMNS rows
    FOR c = 0..LEN(rows[0]) DIV 4 - 1
        FOR r = 0..LEN(rows) - 1
            EQUB mode5_byte(rows[r][4*c..4*c+3])
        NEXT
    NEXT
ENDMACRO

; The game's pictures (src/default.6502inc) are drawn two characters a pixel,
; as a MODE 5 pixel is twice as wide as it is tall, so they look in the
; source as they do on the screen. mode5_pictures turns a list of same-sized
; pictures into their bytes, one picture after another, in one go: as a
; FUNCTION over whole lists rather than a FOR over bytes, it adds a handful of
; entries to the symbol dump rather than one per byte.

; Where each byte's leftmost pixel starts in count pictures of height rows
; of width characters, run together: picture by picture, then a column of
; four pixels (eight characters) at a time, then down the rows.
FUNCTION picture_byte_starts(count, height, width) = FLATTEN(ZIP(ZIP((0..count-1) * height * width)) + ZIP((0..width DIV 8 - 1) * 8) + (0..height-1) * width)

; Pixel n's bits in a byte (n = 0 leftmost), for each pixel's character in
; chars: the colour's high bit in bit 7-n and its low bit in bit 3-n.
FUNCTION pixel_bits(chars, n) = {0, 8, 128, 136}[FIND(CODES(".123"), CODES(chars))] >> n

FUNCTION mode5_pictures(pictures)
    text = CHR(CODES(pictures))
    ASSERT text[0..2..] = text[1..3..], "a pixel is two characters the same"
    ASSERT LEN(text) = LEN(pictures) * LEN(pictures[0]) * LEN(pictures[0][0]), "pictures of different sizes"
    starts = picture_byte_starts(LEN(pictures), LEN(pictures[0]), LEN(pictures[0][0]))
= pixel_bits(text[starts], 0) + pixel_bits(text[starts + 2], 1) + pixel_bits(text[starts + 4], 2) + pixel_bits(text[starts + 6], 3)

; A picture laid out as MODE 5 screen memory: a band of eight rows at a time,
; each band a cell (four pixels across, eight down) after another, left to
; right. Copying it to the screen a band per character row shows it.
MACRO SCREEN_PICTURE rows
    FOR b = 0..LEN(rows) DIV 8 - 1
        FOR c = 0..LEN(rows[0]) DIV 4 - 1
            FOR r = 8*b..8*b+7
                EQUB mode5_byte(rows[r][4*c..4*c+3])
            NEXT
        NEXT
    NEXT
ENDMACRO
